The fix for crbugs 576082223, 580866733 and 578659916 (restricted: "[webcodecs]
Route callbacks to execution context task runners"): chromium/src main commit
bd724a5bc5a82b247f6b3ec086f039e4325e08e9 (main@{#1743484}), merged to the 159
branch as 032ab31330. Its 158 merge (Gerrit 8828129) is pending, as of
8127@{#1899}: its patchset 2 still has a conflict in video_encoder.cc.

WebCodecs' encoder, readback, GPU factory retrieval and ImageDecoderExternal
callbacks were posted to SequencedTaskRunner::GetCurrentDefault(), so they ran
while a page or worker was paused or frozen (e.g. in a nested loop): a renderer
memory-safety risk reachable from a page. The fix routes them through the
execution context's task runners.

This is the main commit's change without its tests, regenerated against 158's
files (8127@{#1899}, which the pending 158 merge's parent matches). 14 of its 15
files are byte-identical to the pending 158 merge's. In video_encoder.cc, the
one hunk that conflicts is resolved as main's change without the
`encode_options` argument, which 158's OnReadbackDone call doesn't have; the rest
of that file matches the 158 merge too. Drop this once 158 gets the fix (check
that the merged change is the same).

